SUMMARY:Historic Mount Pleasant Cemetery
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nThe only autho
 rized cemeteries within York were Anglican or Roman Catholic. Citizens who
  did not belong to either church had no choice but to find burial arrangem
 ents outside York.\n\nThe General Burying Ground received Royal Assent in 
 1826 and land that came to be known as Potters Field was acquired and star
 ted operation soon afterwards. Over time\, additional cemetery lands were 
 added and in 1873\, a new cemetery available to all citizens was establish
 ed. The new cemetery was situated on the farm land of the Cawthra family n
 ear Yonge Street.\n\nThis walk is for all fitness levels. Please dress for
  the weather. This walk will begin and end outside the Yorkminster Park Ba
 ptist Church at 1585 Yonge Street just north of Heath Street.\n\nThis tour
  has a ticket price of $15.00 per person! This tour has space for **11** e
 xplorers\, so if you do plan on attending please secure your tickets early
 .\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when bookin
 g your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:*
 *\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/317325
 914/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261107T121051Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261107T121051Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Thescifibookclub": "https://www.meetup.com/thescifibookclub/events/316438537/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_thescifibookclub
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Sci Fi Book Club
UID:event_316438537@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T065206Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261122T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261122T160000
SUMMARY:Look to Windward - Ian M. Banks
DESCRIPTION:The Sci Fi Book Club\nHi all\,\n\nSo glad to have our Iain M. 
 Banks selection finalized for November. As we’ve discussed previously\, 
 the books in the Culture series are connected\, but don’t necessarily ne
 ed to be read in order. The Club really enjoyed Book 2\, *The Player of Ga
 mes*\, and I’m curious to see where in the universe we land with Book 7\
 , 2000’s *Look to Windward*.\n\n[sophyanempire](https://sophyanempire.wo
 rdpress.com/2012/03/08/look-to-windward-iain-m-banks-orbit-2000/) has a so
 lid review of this entry in the Culture series\, calling *Look to Windward
 * “exciting\, tense\, sad and heroic.” She notes that from there\, “
 the book grows in scope\, showing multiple perspectives\, almost all of th
 em from a non-human alien point of view.”\n\n[The Guardian](https://www.
 theguardian.com/books/2000/sep/02/sciencefictionfantasyandhorror.iainbanks
 ) also has a great review from when the book was first published. Phil Dao
 ust writes that “Banks has tremendous fun with his giant canvas” in *W
 indward*.\n\nTo join a Book Club meeting\, all you will need is YOURSELF. 
 If you haven’t had a chance to finish the book\, we still would love for
  you to join us in the discussion.\n\nNot able to join us in person for ev
 ents? [The Sci Fi Book Club is on Discord](https://discord.gg/B9NMnC2F). J
 oin us and keep the conversation going.\n\nA reminder that Book Club takes
  a break each October\, so while Look to Windward has a fairly large page 
 count\, we’ll essentially have two months to read our pick.\n\nCheers\,\
 n\nJon
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/thescifibookclub/events/316438537/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260906T021855Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260906T021855Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
