SUMMARY:Investing Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T130000
UID:6afdb5b822b92c0041aaa847@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to investing? Learn the basics of this important part of f
 inancial literacy\, including how to save with the goal of investing\, typ
 es of investments\, how to open an account\, types of accounts\, how to av
 oid financial frauds and scams\, and more.\nPresented by Canadian Investme
 nt Regulatory Organization (CIRO)\, a national self-regulatory organizatio
 n that oversees all investment dealers\, mutual fund dealers and trading a
 ctivity on Canada’s debt and equity marketplaces.\nDrop-in. No registrat
 ion required.\nPlease visit the City Hall branch\, or call us at (416) 393
 -7650 if you have any questions.\nToronto Public Library is committed to a
 ccessibility. Please call or email us if you are Deaf or have a disability
  and would like to request an accommodation to participate in this program
 . Please let us know as far in advance as possible and we will do our best
  to meet your request. At least three weeks' notice is preferred. Phone (4
 16) 393-7099 or email\naccessibleservices@tpl.ca\n.
LOCATION:City Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afdb5b822b92c0041aaa847
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
