X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af3515e5ea4c386b3ed438d"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Pre-Show: Bruce Lee Inspired Fight Choreography
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T184500
UID:6af3515e5ea4c386b3ed438d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Aside from inspiring generations of Asian and non-Asians aroun
 d the world with his charm\, witt and passion\, Bruce Lee sparked a martia
 l arts revolution in Hollywood with his explosive fight choreography.\nVet
 eran stunt performer for film and television and former member of the Jack
 ie Chan Stunt Team\, Allen Keng\, will demonstrate a live choreographed fi
 ght sequence inspired by one of Bruce Lee's iconic film scenes. The demons
 tration will be followed by a short Q&A.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nAl
 len Keng is the founder and head of Training Madness Gym where he trains i
 ndividuals in gymnastics\, trampoline\, parkour\, and stunts for film & tv
 . His credits include Pacific Rim\, Shazam!\, and Karate Kid: Legends. He 
 has worked with Idris Elba\, Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson\, and Michelle Yeoh
 .\nAbout Pre-Show Activities:\nPresented before select events\, our Pre-Sh
 ows are all about bringing people together in creative\, fun ways.\nThis p
 re-show is followed by\nJeff Chang: Bruce Lee and the Making of Asian Amer
 ica\n\, which starts at 7pm in the Appel Salon. You can register for that 
 event\nhere\n\, but please note if you wish to attend the pre-event activi
 ty you need to register separately\non this page\n.\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:
 \nLocation:\nBram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (789 Y
 onge Street)\, 2nd floor\nTime:\nDoors open 5:30pm\, Event starts 6:00pm.\
 nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these 
 events to ensure that the greatest number of people have an opportunity to
  attend. Tickets guaranteed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Sea
 ting first come\, first served.\nBar:\nBeer/wine available for purchase (d
 ebit/credit only).\n***\nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Series
 \n\, where we host local and international authors\, artists and thinkers 
 in conversation about their new books and big ideas.\n***\nInformation Col
 lection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the
  Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 
 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program
  registration\, delivery and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted to f
 ill out a brief survey following the program. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answer
 line@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Bram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto 
 Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af3515e5ea4c386b3ed438d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
