SUMMARY:Lessons from Home to “Here”
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T200000
UID:6aaad6f9ca248a002916457f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of Fort York Library's\nEntrepreneur in R
 esidence\n(EIR) service.\nA panel of newcomer professionals\, moderated b
 y Entrepreneur in Residence (Newcomer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, will share the
 ir successful journey from their life at “home” to their new home. Wha
 t are their lessons learned as newcomer entrepreneurs where they can now g
 ive back to their new home and community?\nPanelists include: Katie Duyen
 \, owner of Phin & Go Cafe\; Helena Li\, founder of Oneness Ally\; Sunny
  Verma\, founder of Tutor Bright\; and Dominik Loncar\, Entrepreneur Coach
 \, Futurpreneur\nIn this session:\nBe inspired by established newcomer ent
 repreneurs.\nGain motivation to work on your business and not in your busi
 ness.\nUnderstand and overcome barriers unique to newcomer entrepreneurs\n
 Come early to network from 6-6:30pm!\nTo apply for one-on-one consultation
 s with our resident entrepreneur\, Jean\, please fill out the in-take form
  available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal
  information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under
  the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inform
 ation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and 
 evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can b
 e directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 78
 9 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad6f9ca248a002916457f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
