X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Make A Will with the Ontario Bar Association
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T140000
UID:6ae28506f4d1423e2ce4dcfa@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Make a Will Month and TPL is delighted to host the
  Ontario Bar Association. Learn about the importance of having a will and 
 powers of attorney for you and your family. A member of the\nOntario Bar A
 ssociation\nwho practices Trusts and Estates Law will speak about the elem
 ents of a will\, what happens if you don’t have one\, what are powers of
  attorney\, why they are important and special considerations to keep in m
 ind when preparing your estate and care plans. Note\, this program is for 
 general information only\, not for drafting individual wills.''\nDrop in\,
  No Registration Required.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Room 224
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae28506f4d1423e2ce4dcfa
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
