UID:10003412-1795622400-1795627800@www.culturelink.ca
SUMMARY:Find Your Next Job in Toronto
DESCRIPTION:Newcomer Youth Success: Employment Services  \nFree workshop for newcomers  \nWho Can Participate?    \nThis workshop is for newcomer youth:  Ages 15–30 with permanent residents or convention refugees status. \nDiscover job opportunities in a variety of industries:   \n\nHospitality  \nCustomer Service  \nManufacturing  \nAdministration \n\nWhat You’ll Learn    \n\nDiscover job postings and application links \nLearn how to match your skills to a job \nGet helpful resume writing tips  \nLearn how to prepare for job interviews\n\nBe Prepared and have your resume ready!  \nTo Register:  \nPlease fill this form  \nFor more information\, please contact Olean at 437-225-0568 or email her at oyatsura@culturelink.ca  \nYour Future Starts Here!  \nExplore opportunities\, build your confidence\, and take a step closer to your employment goals. 
URL:https://www.culturelink.ca/event/find-your-next-job-in-toronto/
CATEGORIES:Youth
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.culturelink.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Newcomer-Youth-Success-Web-Icon.png
LOCATION:https://www.culturelink.ca/event/find-your-next-job-in-toronto/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Engineering Engineering Events": "https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/info-session-laidlaw-scholars-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:engineering_engineering_events
X-SOURCE:UofT Engineering
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T170000
DTSTAMP:20261118T215835Z
CREATED:20261118T215835Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261118T215835Z
UID:10004858-1795622400-1795626000@www.engineering.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Info Session: Laidlaw Scholars
DESCRIPTION:The Laidlaw Scholars Programme funds up to 25 academically strong and motivated undergraduate students per cycle and provides 16 months of programming that begins in the winter term of your first scholarship award year and ends in the fall term of your second scholarship award year. \nStudents who are selected to participate in the program will: \n\nConduct a research project of your choice under the supervision of a leading academic while receiving mentoring and developing your academic potential;\nReceive bespoke leadership development training to become a next-generation leader;\nExplore potential meaningful career options while developing transferrable skills\, building confidence\, and expanding breadth of knowledge;\nGrow as a leader in a real-world setting with the Leadership-in-Action project while working with communities for shared progress and long-term impact;\nComplete an international experience\, be it through your research or the Leadership-in-Action experience;\nDevelop your character and master the arts of ethical leadership with a certification from Oxford University;\nConnect with extraordinary peers from world-leading universities; and\nReceive generous funding for all of the above!\n\nLaidlaw Scholars Programme Info Sessions\nLearn more about the Laidlaw Scholars Programme and apply to be a Laidlaw Scholar Cohort 2027 by attending the following info sessions. \nVirtual Info Sessions \n\nWednesday\, November 25\, 2026\, 4:00-5:00 PM\n\n\nThursday\, December 10\, 2026\, 12:00-1:00 PM\n\n\nMonday\, January 18\, 2027\, 10:00-11:00 AM \n\n 
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/info-session-laidlaw-scholars-2/
CATEGORIES:Info sessions
END:VEVENT
