BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/planetary-perspectives-in-knowledge-co-production-between-the-global-south-and-north-reflections-on-the-potential-and-challenges-of-experiential-education/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Planetary perspectives in knowledge co-production between the glob
 al South and North: reflections on the potential and challenges of Experie
 ntial Education
DTSTART:20261125T193000Z
DTEND:20261125T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261120T184600Z
UID:MEC-b41785e01b7f3ae10e9cbdb6dc452ed0@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261125T193000Z
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/1
 1/PerspectiveEvent@2x.png
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp\; Urban Change
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261120
DESCRIPTION:This presentation introduces an innovative approach to experie
 ntial education and planetary learning\, developed within a long-standing 
 research partnership between the University of Antioquia in Medellín\, Co
 lombia\, and the University of Education in Bern\, Switzerland. The approa
 ch draws on Latin American critical theory and on the experience of Colomb
 ia’s Movimiento Pedagógico Nacional\, a large-scale social movement of 
 the 1980s and 1990s which organized so-called National Educational Expedit
 ions: researchers and university professors\, activists\, school teachers 
 and students explored together the relation between neoliberal educational
  restructuring and the sharpening sociospatial inequality and violence in 
 the country.\nTransnational Educational Expeditions formed the core of our
  approach to experiential education. In these expeditions\, a binational t
 eam of practitioners\, researchers and students\, made up of equal numbers
  from both partner universities\, jointly carried out ethnographic researc
 h\, first in Switzerland and then in Colombia. Through these expeditions\,
  we explored how public schooling contributes both to reproducing and to t
 ransforming urban inequality in contexts of migration in the two countries
 .\nThe approach is innovative in that it examines social fields in Colombi
 a and Switzerland through each other\, making the systematic contrast of n
 ationally situated perspectives a productive resource in the co-production
  of knowledge.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261120
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/planetary-perspectives-in-knowledge-co-
 production-between-the-global-south-and-north-reflections-on-the-potential
 -and-challenges-of-experiential-education/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
