DESCRIPTION:In the second installment of our virtual speaker series\, Kath
 erine Nastovski (Associate Professor in Global Work and Labour Studies at 
 York) revisits examples in Canadian labour movement history to ask what ra
 dical workers’ education is not\, and what separates initiatives that ac
 commodate existing inequalities from those that help workers build collect
 ive power and solidarity across borders.\n
