SUMMARY: 2026 Mulan International Film Festival
DESCRIPTION:From November 21 to December 3\, join the 7th Mulan Internati
 onal Film Festival at Toronto’s Innis Town Hall. As the largest film fest
 ival dedicated to Chinese-language cinema in North America\, Mulan brings
  restored classics and new voices to the big screen.\n\n\nOpening night p
 resents the Canadian premiere of the 4K restoration of Patrick TAM’s Love
  Massacre\, starring Brigitte LIN. The festival closes with the North Ame
 rican premiere of CHONG Keat Aun’s Golden Horse Award-winning Mother Bhum
 i\, winner of Best Leading Actress for FAN Bingbing\, Best Cinematography
  and Best Original Film Song.\n\n\nDiscover six features and nine shorts 
 from emerging filmmakers in the Fountainhead competition programme\, and 
 vote for your favourites. Other highlights include the world premiere of 
 the new 4K restoration of Clara LAW’s Farewell\, China\, starring Maggie 
 CHEUNG and Tony LEUNG Ka-Fai\, and On Canvas\, On Stage\, a complete retr
 ospective of QIU Jiongjiong’s films\, including A New Old Play and Madame
 .\n\n\nFestival Packs and individual tickets\, starting at $10 plus proce
 ssing fees\, are now on sale.\n\n\nScreening times vary by day.
CATEGORIES:Film,Innis-Town-Hall,Festival
