UID:MEC-4c7e17f10bce99f0c3df0f414eb9165c@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261202T190000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:16 Days of Activism,Students,The Centre
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261119
DESCRIPTION:As part of the 16 Days of Activism Against Gender-Based Violen
 ce\, this creative reflection space invites participants to explore healin
 g\, resilience and community care through journaling and spoken word. \nPa
 rticipants can write\, reflect\, and\, if they choose\, share their words 
 in a supportive environment that honours survivors’ experiences while we
 lcoming all members of the community. \nTogether\, we will consider how st
 orytelling\, creativity and collective action can contribute to a safer an
 d more equitable world. \nDate: Wednesday\, December 2\nTime: 2 – 3 p.m
 .\nLocation: to be provided upon registration\nSpace is limited to 10 part
 icipants.\nClick here to register \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261119
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/voices-of-hope-journaling-spoken-word-c
 ircle/
