BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/national-day-of-remembrance-and-action-on-violence-against-women-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:National Day of Remembrance and Action on Violence Against Women
DTSTART:20261203T150000Z
DTEND:20261203T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20261120T172300Z
UID:MEC-07cb5b5337dc005c70dc51527a70162a@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261203T150000Z
SEQUENCE:1
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261120
DESCRIPTION:December 6 is the National Day of Remembrance and Action on Vi
 olence Against Women\, a time to remember the lives lost and acknowledge t
 he ongoing impact of gender-based violence. As we reflect\, we also reaffi
 rm our collective responsibility to stand with survivors\, raise awareness
 \, and confront the deep-rooted norms that sustain violence and hate.​\n
 York University will hold a memorial ceremony in honour of the 14 women ki
 lled at Polytechnique Montréal on December 6\, 1989: Geneviève Bergeron\
 , Hélène Colgan\, Nathalie Croteau\, Barbara Daigneault\, Anne-Marie Edw
 ard\, Maud Haviernick\, Maryse Laganière\, Maryse Leclair\, Anne-Marie Le
 may\, Sonia Pelletier\, Michèle Richard\, Annie St-Arneault\, Annie Turco
 tte\, and Barbara Klucznik-Widajewicz.​\nThe event will take place at th
 e Bergeron Centre for Engineering Excellence on Dec. 3\, 2026\, from 10 to
  11:00 a.m. Community members at Glendon and Markham Campuses are encourag
 ed to gather for the livestream at their respective locations: the Ballroo
 m in Glendon Manor and room MK2050 at Markham. The memorial ceremony\, alo
 ng with other events planned for the 16 Days of Activism Against Gender-
 Based Violence\, aims to honour those who have been lost and inspire the c
 ommunity to take meaningful action and support those in need.​\nIn solid
 arity\, please consider wearing a white ribbon as a symbol of your commitm
 ent to ending gender-based violence. Ribbons will be available at the memo
 rial ceremony and live stream viewing locations on Dec. 3.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261120
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/national-day-of-remembrance-and-action-
 on-violence-against-women-2/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
