SUMMARY:3D Design: SculptGL
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T190000
UID:6aff64bc22b92c0041ab07bb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Get started on the basics of using SculptGL\, a browser-based 
 3D sculpting and design tool. In this class\, you will:\nCreate a simple 3
 D sculpt using symmetry\, masking\, and clean-up tools\, and export your m
 odel for sharing or 3D printing.\nLearn how to navigate the SculptGL works
 pace\, menus\, and options (including camera orbit/pan/zoom controls and c
 ommon view shortcuts).\nUse essential sculpting tools such as Brush\, Infl
 ate\, Smooth\, Flatten\, Crease\, Drag/Move\, plus Masking and Transform t
 o shape and refine a model.\nAdd basic surface finish and color with verte
 x painting / material controls\, then preview your model with different re
 nder options.\nPrerequisites: Mouse and keyboarding skills required.\nScul
 ptGL website:\nhttps://stephaneginier.com/scu...
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, 2nd Floor\, Far back room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aff64bc22b92c0041ab07bb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
