SUMMARY:Portrait perfection workshop -3 hour
DESCRIPTION:The Toronto Photography Group\n## Titckets available at our we
 bsite- www.wtpg.ngo -\n\n[https://www.wtpg.ngo/event-details/sale-portrait
 -perfection-photo-lighting-workshop-w-anjali](https://www.wtpg.ngo/event-d
 etails/sale-portrait-perfection-photo-lighting-workshop-w-anjali)\n\n## Ti
 me & Location\n\nDec 03\, 2026\, 7:00 PM – 10:00 PM\nRevprint Studio 205
 \, 146 Thirtieth St\, Etobicoke\, ON M8W 3C4\, Canada\n\n## About the even
 t\n\n### **Studio Portrait Lighting Workshop**\n\n**Date:** Thursday\, Dec
 ember 3rd 2026\n**Time:** 7:00 PM – 10:00 PM\n**Instructor:** *Phil Suth
 erland* – Elinchrom Ambassador & Executive Director\, West Toronto Photo
 graphy Group\nModel Anjali- gallery of images from previous workshop\n\n* 
 ![](https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1eaf19_b0ffafd7c26d4239b3325eeb9fdd
 1353~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920\,h_1097\,al_c\,q_90\,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01\,enc_a
 uto/1eaf19_b0ffafd7c26d4239b3325eeb9fdd1353~mv2.jpg)\n\n**Lighting Equipme
 nt:** Provided by **Elinchrom**\n**Location:** Revprint Studio 205 - 146 T
 hirtierth street unit 205\n**Workshop Size:** Limited to **6 participants*
 *\n\n#### **Workshop Overview**\n\nJoin us for a fun and informative **Por
 trait Perfection photography lighting and shooting workshop** designed to 
 help you build skills and portfolio images and technical skills in the art
  of portrait lighting. Whether you’re new to studio photography or looki
 ng to refine your lighting technique\, this hands-on session will guide yo
 u through essential tools\, setups\, and creative lighting approaches.\nTh
 is **three-hour\, small-group workshop** ensures plenty of individual atte
 ntion\, shooting time\, and opportunities to ask questions.\n\n#### **What
  You’ll Learn**\n\n1. **Studio Gear** A detailed overview of lighting eq
 uipment\, modifiers\, and how we will use them for each lighting set up we
  build as a group ..\n2. **Studio Design & Setup**Understand how to plan a
 nd use studio space efficiently for portrait sessions.\n3. **Modifiers & L
 ight Quality** Explore how different modifiers affect your images as we ut
 ilize the Rotolaux modifiers from Elinchrom in studio.\n4. **Building a Li
 ghting Setup** As a group we will step-by-step construct professional port
 rait lighting setups using Elinchrom lights and modifiers.\n5. **Hands-On 
 Shooting Practice** Photograph our model Lilli in **multiple lighting setu
 ps that create strong and elegant lighting** —each participant will have
  one-on-one shooting time and instructor feedback. You will get some stunn
 ing images for your portfolio from the small group 3 hour portrait perfect
 ion lighting workshop\n\n#### **Who Should Attend**\n\nThis workshop is id
 eal for photographers of all skill levels who want to:\n\n* Learn or refre
 sh the fundamentals of portrait and studio lighting or pick up a few new t
 ricks\n* Get hands-on experience with professional lighting equipment from
  Elinchrom\n* Practice creating and refining lighting setups that you can 
 use to WOW clients\n* Build confidence shooting portraits in a studio envi
 ronment while updating your portfolio\n\n#### **What to Bring**\n\n* A **D
 SLR or mirrorless camera** with a working hot-shoe\n* **Fresh batteries** 
 and **formatted memory cards**\n* Your **favourite lens** (anything betwee
 n 10mm–200mm works great)\n* Curiosity\, creativity\, and your passion f
 or photography!\n\n#### **What’s Included**\n\n* Professional instructio
 n and lighting gear provided by **Elinchrom**\n* Access to a variety of li
 ght modifiers: reflectors\, umbrellas\, softboxes\, grids\, snoots\, and b
 eauty dishes\n* A safe\, supportive\, and professional environment to lear
 n and network\n* Dedicated time with the model for individual shooting opp
 ortunities\n\n\\*\\*Time is money\, and we value yours.\\*\\*That’s why 
 we keep our workshops efficient\, informative\, and fun—so you leave ins
 pired\, informed\, and ready to light your next portrait session like a pr
 o.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-photography-group/events/3175
 17526/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261120T194212Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261120T194212Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
