SUMMARY:Anthropology in Relation: Reciprocal Knowledges\, Connecting Commu
 nities\, and Shared Futures
DTSTART:20261204T133000Z
DTEND:20261204T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20261119T163100Z
UID:MEC-05af5f0beb11c1a6fdf5983c4a243a0e@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261204T133000Z
SEQUENCE:4
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,LA&amp\;PS 
 Department of Anthropology
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261119
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a day of presentations\, discussions and networkin
 g that explores how relationality and collaboration shape anthropological 
 research and community engagement. The symposium will showcase student pro
 jects\, research collaborations and experiences working with community par
 tners\, while creating opportunities for undergraduate students\, graduate
  students\, alumni and community members to connect and learn from one ano
 ther.\nBy bringing these voices and experiences into conversation\, the sy
 mposium invites participants to consider how shared knowledges\, reciproca
 l relationships and collective action can expand anthropology’s reach an
 d build connected futures.\nAll members of the York community are welcome 
 to attend.\nRSVP Here\n
