SUMMARY: Killer B Cinema Presents: Don’t Open Till Christmas
DESCRIPTION:On Friday\, December 4th\, join us for a little bit of Christ
 mas Horror! Don’t Open Till Christmas. Oh… and Caroline Munro!!!\n\nAdvan
 ced tickets are $5 (plus Eventbrite service fee)\; tickets at the door ar
 e $8 (Space is limited\, and tickets sell out fast)!\n\nDoors open at 7:3
 0 pm\, and the movie begins at 8:00.\n\nTicket link: https://www.eventbri
 te.ca/e/2004522884909?aff=oddtdtcreator https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/20045
 22884909?aff=oddtdtcreator\n\nTrailer: www.youtube.com/watch?v=c6qIdDHqSf
 M https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c6qIdDHqSfM\n\n*NO outside food or drin
 ks\; please buy food and drinks from the venue.\n\n*All films have closed
  captioning.\n\nMovie info:\n\nForget peace on Earth and goodwill to all 
 men. This Christmas\, Santa is on someone's naughty list!\n\nChristmas in
  London has taken a decidedly bloody turn. A mysterious killer with a ser
 ious grudge against Father Christmas is stalking the streets\, brutally d
 ispatching anyone unfortunate enough to be wearing a red suit and white b
 eard. As the bodies pile up\, Scotland Yard races to uncover the identity
  of the murderer before another unsuspecting Santa meets a particularly g
 ruesome end. With the festive season fast approaching\, it seems nobody d
 ressed as jolly old Saint Nick is safe!\n\nReleased in 1984\, Don't Open 
 Till Christmas is a gloriously sleazy slice of British holiday horror\, p
 acked with outrageous murders\, questionable decisions\, and all the wond
 erfully bizarre excesses of 1980s exploitation cinema. Directed by and st
 arring Edmund Purdom\, with an appearance by cult horror favourite Caroli
 ne Munro\, this delightfully trashy Christmas slasher offers plenty of go
 re\, unintentional laughs\, and festive mayhem. It's everything you could
  want from a Killer B Cinema Christmas screening\, a little naughty\, a l
 ot bloody\, and most definitely not suitable for the whole family!\n\nKil
 ler B Cinema invites you to celebrate the holidays the B-movie way. Just 
 remember: whatever you do\, DON'T OPEN TILL CHRISTMAS! Oh\, and did I men
 tion Caroline Munro?\n\nInfo about See-Scape:\n\nOur movies will be shown
  on the second floor! There are two bars available in See-Scape. The bar 
 on the second floor is open during our event and is cash-only. Debit/Cred
 it purchases are available on the main floor.\n\nSee-Scape also has an am
 azing menu. To learn more about See-Scape\, please click here! www.seesca
 peto.com/ https://www.seescapeto.com/\n\nSee-Scape is located at 347 Keel
 e Street (the closest intersection is Keele/Dundas) and is easily accessi
 ble via TTC. (from Keele Station or Dundas West Station)\n\nParking: Ther
 e is a Green P parking lot beside See-Scape and a few other paid parking 
 lots nearby.\n\nEach month\, join Lizzie Violet & Zoltan Du Lac for kille
 r B-moves from the 1930s to the present!\n\nPlease like our Facebook page
  and Instagram @killerbcinema so you don’t miss an invite.\n\nThank you t
 o See-Scape and their staff! They make our monthly event extra unforgetta
 ble!\n\nWe hope to see you at See-Scape.\n\n
CATEGORIES:Film,See-Scape
