SUMMARY:The Publication Process\, With Author Danielle Younge-Ullman
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T150000
UID:6b00e0cc0ad4ed003a04cc8f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Would you like to learn about the writing and publication proc
 ess?\n​Danielle Younge-Ullman\, author of award-winning novels\,\nEveryt
 hing Beautiful is Not Ruined\n\, and\nHe Must Like You\n\,\ndiscusses some
  of the events that inspired these stories\, and the publication process b
 ehind them.\nShe will discuss the methods a writer can use to improve thei
 r craft\, and her best practices when it comes to getting her work publish
 ed.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Fourth Floor\, Jack Rabinovitch Room
