 s\, sports\, presentations\, or everyday challenges\, this program will he
 lp you show up ready.\nFacilitated by Stephanie Guerra. Stephanie is a Cer
 tified Mental Performance Consultant (CMPC) with\nMindset First\n\, helpin
 g youth build confidence and find success.\nThis workshop is part of the T
 een Social Health and Wellness programming. Generously supported by The Es
 tate of Claudia Krawchuk.\nNo registration is required. Drop-in only.\nMon
 day\, December 7\nFairview Library\n416-395-5750\n35 Fairview Mall Drive\,
  North York\, ON M2J 4S4\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth
  Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\, whe
 re helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offere
 d daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find ou
 t more.\nAccessibility\nLive or automated closed captioning\, sign languag
 e interpretation\, intervenor services\, or attendant services are availab
 le upon request. Please submit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to
 :\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.
