DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T163000
UID:6aff629104009d003389bc93@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ages 8+\nLearn to create your first 3D project\, design a pers
 onalized item and choose colours to print it. TinkerCAD is an easy to lear
 n and free browser based 3D design program from Autodesk.\nIn this class\,
  you will:\nLearn how to navigate the TinkerCAD workspace\, menus\, and vi
 ews (zoom\, pan\, rotate).\nBuild a clean\, printable design using accurat
 e sizing\, rulers and measurements\, and simple design best practices.\nCu
 stomize your project with text\, cutouts using the Hole tool\, and colour 
 choices.\nExport your finished model (STL) so it can be 3D printed or shar
 ed.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, 2nd Floor\, Far back room
