BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aff191cd164f314d93cb25a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Hackathon: AI for Digital Rights
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T180000
UID:6aff191cd164f314d93cb25a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Digital rights are the freedoms we should all have online\, in
 cluding the ability to access information\, protect our privacy\, stay saf
 e from scams\, participate in our communities and engage in a language we 
 understand.\nDuring the week of Digital International Rights Days\, take p
 art in a full-day hackathon where you'll work in a team to imagine and des
 ign a software prototype that advances digital rights\, then experiment wi
 th AI-assisted coding to build it. Explore AI tools and discover how they 
 can help build or maintain software that serves communities. Apps for your
  community\, by your community.\nPlease bring your own computer. No coding
  experience is required\, but participants should have mouse\, keyboarding
  and internet skills.\nCreate your own team (6 people max) or join one thr
 ough our matching process. All participants\nmust register individually\n\
 , regardless of whether they have already formed a team. After registering
 \, you will receive a questionnaire to indicate whether you are part of an
  existing team or would like to be matched to one. The questionnaire will 
 help us understand your skills\, interests and preferences to support team
  formation.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice\n: The personal informatio
 n on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public
  Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will 
 only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation.
  Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed 
