SUMMARY:FRESH Movie Saturdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T130000
UID:6ac7f0c229c3d600332e9eaf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Come join us every Saturday for screenings of your favourite movies. In ad
 dition to this\, enjoy cuddles with a therapy dog! Therapy dog Goose visi
 ts Fort York Branch on alternate Saturdays from 11:00AM-12:00PM.\nWe'll b
 e showing the following films:\nNov 14 - Africa-An Cats\nNov 21 - The Odd 
 Life of Timothy Green\nNov 28 - Little Big League\nDec 5 – Dog Man\nDec
  12 – HitPi\nDec 19 - A Muppet Christmas Carol\nJan 2 - The Incredible 
 Journey (1963)\nJan 9 - Trolls Band Together\nJan 16 - Pete's Dragon\nJan 
 23 - Turner and Hooch\nJan 30 - Soul\nFeb 6 - The Odd Life of Timothy Gree
 n\nFeb 13 - The Parent Trap (1961)\nFeb 20 - Escape to Witch Mountain (197
 5)\nFeb 27 - Never Cry Wolf\nDrop-ins are welcome.\nThis program is in col
 laboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Urban Living Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7f0c229c3d600332e9eaf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af475ee08e64c003ab881b4"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Cooking with Spirit: Stories\, Flavours\, and Traditions from Indi
 genous Fusion Cuisine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T120000
UID:6af475ee08e64c003ab881b4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this talk\, Chef David Wolfman will take the audience on a 
 culinary and cultural journey through the pages of his cookbook\,\nCooking
  With the Wolfman\n. Drawing from the traditions of the Xaxli’p First Na
 tion and his decades of professional culinary expertise\, David will share
  stories behind the making of select recipes an explore how Indigenous foo
 ds connect us to the land\, to community\, and to sustainable living. Part
 icipants will also learn how cooking can be an act of reconciliation and c
 ultural preservation.\nAt the end and of the program\, David will lead a Q
 &A session and share food samples with attendees.\nRegistration Required.\
 nDavid Wolfman\, from Xaxli’p First Nation\, has reshaped Canada's gastr
 onomic landscape and global perceptions of Indigenous and North American c
 uisine. David was the first of many to have an Indigenous catering enterpr
 ise in Toronto. Outside of the kitchen\, Chef Wolfman shares his love of f
 ood\, family and friendship through education. He leads workshops on Indig
 enous culinary practices\, cultural tourism\, and economical family food b
 udgeting. He has done so at youth conferences\, business conventions\, and
  through his role as a Culinary Arts professor at George Brown College. Ch
 ef Wolfman was also an executive producer and host of "Cooking with the Wo
 lfman" on APTN from 1999 to 2017\, where he shared Indigenous Fusion foods
  to viewers across Canada. Chef Wolfman lives in Toronto and enjoys being 
 walked by his Boston Terrier.
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af475ee08e64c003ab881b4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
