SUMMARY: Monty Alexander – Borderless Jazz 2026
DESCRIPTION:From Kingston to the international jazz stage\, Monty Alexand
 er brings the sounds of Jamaica and the traditions of American jazz toget
 her in a special holiday concert in Toronto.\n\nThe Grammy-nominated pian
 ist tells his musical story through jazz\, ska and reggae\, tracing a car
 eer that began in Jamaica and led to collaborations with figures includin
 g Ray Brown\, Milt Jackson\, Quincy Jones\, Dizzy Gillespie and Sonny Rol
 lins. For this performance\, Alexander is joined by Lorin Cohen on acoust
 ic bass\, Joshua Thomas on guitar and electric bass\, and Jason Brown on 
 drums.\n\nTickets: $45 to $125 at http://tickets.smallworldmusic.com/e/s-
 w-m-jazz-monty\n\nPresented by Small World Music as part of Borderless Ja
 zz 2026\, in partnership with The Creative School Chrysalis.
CATEGORIES:Concert,The-Creative-School-Chrysalis
