DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively discussion about the selected book of the
  month in a welcoming and friendly space. Everyone is welcome. Get your ph
 ysical copy in-branch at the Reference Desk or borrow an eBook/eAudiobook 
 copy by downloading the Libby app on your mobile device or tablet.\nRegist
 er to receive email reminders about upcoming book club dates.\nOctober 28 
 -\nDrive your Plow Over the Bones of the Dead\nby Olga Tokarczuk\nNovember
  25 -\nIf I Survive You\nby Jonathan Escoffery\nDecember 16 -\nHorse\nby 
 Geraldine Brooks\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information
  on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public 
 Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will o
 nly be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. 
 Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed t
 o Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Stre
 et\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Located in Room A on the third floor
