BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1a68d65abe8002a77dd16"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Sanko Speaks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T140000
UID:6aa1a68d65abe8002a77dd16@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A free\, culturally affirming drop-in program for adults that 
 promotes mental wellness through creative activities\, discussion\, and he
 althy coping strategies. Guided by the concept of Sankofa\, participants e
 xplore connections between past experiences and present wellbeing while bu
 ilding skills for managing stress and supporting mental health. Activities
  vary based on community interests and needs.\nThis program is in collabor
 ation with\nTAIBU Community Health Centre.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1a68d65abe8002a77dd16
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Preschool": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa9fcd23dd190003e724a0c"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_preschool
SUMMARY:Maison des bébés
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T113000
UID:6aa9fcd23dd190003e724a0c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Un programme spécialement conçu pour les bébés de 0 à 18 
 mois et leurs accompagnateurs.\nChanter des chansons et des comptines à v
 otre bébé favorise le développement du langage tout en partageant un mo
 ment amusant et chaleureux.\nLes comptines avec gestes encouragent égalem
 ent les tout‑petits à bouger et à explorer selon leur stade de dévelo
 ppement.\nCe programme est offert en partenariat avec le\nCentre francopho
 ne du Grand Toronto.\nAccessibilité:\nLe sous-titrage en direct ou automa
 tique\, l’interprétation en langue des signes\, les services\nd’inter
 venant\, ou les services d’accompagnement sont disponibles sur demande. 
 Veuillez\nsoumettre votre demande au moins deux semaines à l’avance à 
 : tpl.ca/accessibility-events\nA program specially designed for babies age
 d 0 to 18 months and their caregivers.\nSinging songs and rhymes to your b
 aby helps support language development while sharing a fun and warm moment
  together.\nAction rhymes also encourage little ones to move and explore a
 ccording to their developmental stage.\nThis program is offered in partner
 ship with the\nCentre francophone du Grand Toronto.
LOCATION:Danforth/Coxwell
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa9fcd23dd190003e724a0c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af4bf7a4896360041d0d65d"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Sewing Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T120000
UID:6af4bf7a4896360041d0d65d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to learn to sew or would like a refresher on how to use a
  sewing machine? Our intro to sewing course will cover the basics of threa
 ding the machine\, basic stitches and more. We will be creating a small po
 uch. All materials will be provided.\nChildren under 13 must be accompanie
 d by an adult.\nRegistration is required for this class and begins Decembe
 r 3\, 2026 at 12:30 pm.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 mi
 nutes of the start of the program.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
 information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliver
 y and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information
  can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-598
 1\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af4bf7a4896360041d0d65d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
