BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ada7d6b8a335b6ae5ca0029"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Club de lecture théâtre avec le Théâtre français de Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T193000
UID:6ada7d6b8a335b6ae5ca0029@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:La Bibliothèque publique de Toronto et le\nThéâtre françai
 s de Toronto\ns'associent pour créer un club de lecture théâtre. Ce ren
 dez-vous mensuel est l'occasion de discuter et d'explorer des scènes myth
 iques ayant marqué le monde du théâtre. Avec\nGeorges Som\n\, médiateu
 r culturel\, nous essayerons de comprendre les enjeux de ces scènes\, de 
 découvrir leurs sens et de partager nos sentiments sur leurs auteurs et a
 utrices. Chacun est le bienvenu au club\, qu'il soit néophyte ou amateur 
 de théâtre confirmé. Les seuls prérequis pour participer sont la curio
 sité et le plaisir d'échanger autour du théâtre !\nAu mois de décembr
 e\, nous allons discuter un extrait de la pièce\nEn attendant Godot\nde S
 amuel Beckett. Deux vagabonds\, Vladimir et Estragon\, se retrouvent sur 
 une route de campagne\, près d'un arbre\, à la tombée de la nuit. Est-c
 e bien le jour et l'heure pour attendre Godot. Arrivent Pozzo\, un homme a
 utoritaire\, le propriétaire des lieux\, avec un Knouk\, un sous homme te
 nu en laisse.\nInformation Collection Notice\n:\nThe personal information 
 on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public L
 ibraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will on
 ly be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Q
 uestions about how the library handles your information can be directed to
  Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\nACCESSIBILITÉ\nLe sous-titrage en direct ou automat
 ique\, l’interprétation en langue des signes\, les services d’interve
 nant\, ou les services d’accompagnement sont disponibles sur demande. Ve
 uillez soumettre votre demande au moins deux semaines à l’avance à :\n
 tpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Discussion Room\, 3e étage
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ada7d6b8a335b6ae5ca0029
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad7d1f59dbc2b002c8fec9d"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Shannon Kyles: What Our Buildings Say About Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T200000
UID:6ad7d1f59dbc2b002c8fec9d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Shannon Kyles discusses the history of architecture in Ontario
  and what it says about the people who have built this province. Starting 
 with the Indigenous people\, going through the first century of European c
 ontact\, through the 20th century wars\, democratic policies that resulted
 \, and finally onto the 21st century speculative housing practice.\nProfes
 sor Shannon Kyles is the author of ​\nThe Story of Ontario Architecture\
 n. She has written and published articles on architecture\, taught History
  of Ontario architecture for 42 years at Mohawk College and online for uni
 versities\, and has served on the board of the Architectural Conservancy o
 f Ontario for 15 years.\nRegistration encouraged for event reminders and p
 lanning. Register online at tpl.ca\, by calling 416-393-7674\, or in perso
 n at Bloor/Gladstone branch. Drop-ins also welcome.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad7d1f59dbc2b002c8fec9d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6acfe54829c3d600332fefe5"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 6: Use Gmail
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T193000
UID:6acfe54829c3d600332fefe5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to use Gmail\, Google’s free web-based email service.\
 nIn this sixth session you will:\nPractice basic email functions: send\, r
 ead\, reply\, forward\, delete email\, and attach files\nReview how spam a
 nd junk mail work\nUpon completion of this class students will have a basi
 c understanding of how to use email.\nInstructions on how to set up and ma
 nage your own free Gmail account are included in the handout.\nPrerequisit
 es: Basic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with de
 monstrations\nNo Registration\nDrop-ins welcome until capacity is reached.
LOCATION:Forest Hill\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6acfe54829c3d600332fefe5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
