SUMMARY:What is Artificial Intelligence?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261221T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261221T143000
UID:6aff6b55e4f7a1002c0915ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI technologies have become increasingly prevalent in many asp
 ects of modern life\, including healthcare\, finance\, transportation\, an
 d entertainment. Some examples of AI applications include virtual assistan
 ts like Siri and Alexa\, self-driving cars\, fraud detection systems\, and
  personalized recommendations in online shopping. Come join this beginner 
 in-person class to learn what AI is\, how it learns and predicts outcomes\
 , considerations when using GenAI applications\, and how the Internet of T
 hings (IOT) applies to AI.\nQuestions and discussions will be encouraged\n
 Accessibility\nToronto Public Library is committed to accessibility. Pleas
 e call or email us if you have a request for accommodation. Please let us 
 know as far in advance as possible and we will do our best to meet your re
 quest. Phone 416-393-7009 or email accessibilityservices@tpl.ca.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, 2nd Floor\, Far back room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aff6b55e4f7a1002c0915ad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
