SUMMARY: Pet Shop Boys - a Toronto Tribute Day
DESCRIPTION:We'll run through ALL the bigs hit a in a crazy fun-filled tw
 o hours! SATURDAY / Boxing Day.\n\nEarly show - 3pm! FREE.\n\n\nImmerse y
 ourself in the BIG SCREEN / BIG SOUND fun + join a whole pub full of othe
 r Pet Shop Boys fans! FANTASTIC food and drink specials.\n\n\nPET SHOPS B
 OYS VIDEO TRIBUTE DAY – BOXING DAY IN TORONTO!\n\nBoxing Day just got leg
 endary!\n\n\nVIDEO SONG LIST:\n\n\n\nTop 15 Pet Shop Boys Songs (by popul
 arity/streams + chart success)\n\n  1. West End Girls (1985/86) — Their b
 reakthrough\; UK #1 and US #1. Iconic synth-pop with hip-hop and literary
  influences.\n  2. Always on My Mind (1987) — Cover of the Elvis classic 
 that became their Christmas #1 in the UK.\n  3. It’s a Sin (1987) — UK #1
 \; dramatic\, theatrical anthem about guilt and Catholic upbringing.\n  4
 . Go West (1993) — Village People cover\; UK #2. Anthemic and frequently 
 used in sports contexts.\n  5. Domino Dancing (1988) — Latin-tinged dance
 -pop\; UK #7. Marked the end of their early “imperial phase” of #1s.\n  6
 . What Have I Done to Deserve This? (with Dusty Springfield) (1987) — UK 
 #2\; classic duet.\n  7. New York City Boy (1999) — UK #14\; later-period
  disco-pop hit.\n  8. Suburbia (1986) — UK #8\; cinematic take on suburba
 n boredom and rebellion.\n  9. Opportunities (Let’s Make Lots of Money) (
 1986) — UK #11\; satirical yuppie anthem often misunderstood as sincere.\
 n 10. Heart (1988) — UK #1\; pure upbeat pop.\n 11. Se a vida é (That’s t
 he Way Life Is) (1996) — UK #8\; Brazilian-influenced track from Bilingua
 l.\n 12. Rent (1987) — UK #8\; elegant\, melancholic look at a transactio
 nal relationship.\n 13. Love Comes Quickly (1986) — UK #19\; lush early s
 ingle.\n 14. Left to My Own Devices (1988) — UK #4\; orchestral\, camp\, 
 and self-reflective.\n 15. Being Boring (1990) — UK #20\; widely regarded
  as one of their finest (often ranked #1 critically)\, reflecting on yout
 h\, loss\, and the AIDS crisis.\n\n... and many more!\n\n\n\nFREE - RSVP 
 here: www.eventbrite.ca/e/pet-shop-boys-boxing-day-video-tribute-day-earl
 y-show-3pm-tickets-2004648709253?aff=oddtdtcreator https://www.eventbrite
 .ca/e/pet-shop-boys-boxing-day-video-tribute-day-early-show-3pm-tickets-2
 004648709253?aff=oddtdtcreator
CATEGORIES:DJ/Club/Rave,Cat's-Cradle,Listening-Party
