X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Aga Khan Museum": "https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2027-winter-clay-tile-workshop/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Aga Khan Museum": "https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2027-winter-clay-tile-workshop/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:agakhan_museum
SUMMARY:Clay Tile Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270103T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270103T110000
UID:clay-tile-workshop-2027-01-03t11-00-00-05-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/11
 /Clay_Paid_Workshop_Shirin_Divanbeigi11-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scal
 ed.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Experiment with clay and craft your own unique tile in this ha
 nds-on workshop designed for both beginners and art enthusiasts.\n\nGuided
  by our Museum Educators\, participants will explore shaping\, designing\,
  and decorating techniques inspired by ceramic works in the Aga Khan Museu
 m’s Collections. Learn how patterns and motifs have been used for centur
 ies across the Islamic world\, and experiment with tools and textures to b
 ring your vision to life. You’ll leave with a one-of-a-kind creation tha
 t blends traditional inspiration with your own creativity.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2027-winter-clay-tile-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Aga Khan Museum": "https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2027-winter-fasayfisa-mosaic-workshop/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:agakhan_museum
SUMMARY:Fasayfisa’: Introduction to Mosaic Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270103T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270103T110000
UID:fasayfisa-introduction-to-mosaic-workshop-2027-01-03t11-00-00-05-00@ag
 akhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/11
 /Mosaic-Coaster_PaidWorkshop_MadalinaRaduta2-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000
 -scaled.jpeg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Discover the beauty and meaning behind Fasayfisa’ — an Ara
 bic term for small\, colourful pieces of marble or stone arranged side by 
 side to form a unified design.\n\nThrough this hands-on workshop\, partici
 pants will create a small ornament using vibrant glass tiles\, inspired by
  the intricate patterns found in Islamic art and architecture. Drawing fro
 m examples in the Aga Khan Museum Collections\, explore how these repeatin
 g designs embody harmony\, balance\, and creativity\, a tradition that has
  flourished for centuries.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2027-winter-fasayfisa-mosaic-worksh
 op/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
