BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardinermuseum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/wheel-throwing-stoneware-beginner-winter-2027/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270104T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270301T163000
DTSTAMP:20261105T193826Z
CREATED:20261103T214845Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261105T193826Z
UID:148411-1799069400-1803918600@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Wheel Throwing: Stoneware (Beginner)
DESCRIPTION:Wheel Throwing: Stoneware (Beginner)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Mondays January 4 to March 1\, 2027\n1:30 pm – 4:30 pm \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nFor ages 18+ \n\nUsing stoneware clay\, learn basic wheel throwing techniques—centering\, opening\, and pulling up the walls—to create cylinders and bowls. Experiment with various types of surface decoration and exciting glaze combinations on both functional and sculptural pieces. This 8-week class is designed for beginners as well as those wanting to reconnect with clay and learn the fundamentals of making pottery. \n\nThis class includes a 10kg bag of stoneware clay\, and access to glazes and underglazes. Additional bags of clay can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $434\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $510\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: January 4\, 11\, 18\, 25\, February 1\, 8\, 22\, March 1\nNo class February 15 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Week 1: Intro to wedging\, centering\, cylinders\nWeek 2: Trimming; Throwing bowls\nWeek 3: Intro to carving\, texturing\, and underglaze techniques\nWeek 4: Glazing\nWeek 5: Throwing mugs and vessels\nWeek 6: Throwing recap and trimming\nWeek 7: Refining work\nWeek 8: Glazing \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nUsing the pottery wheel may cause serious injury to a person who has a pacemaker. Consult a physician before use.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Audrey Mah\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Audrey Mah is a contemporary ceramic artist living and working in Toronto. She studied visual arts with an interest in Sculpture/Ceramics at the University of Waterloo\, and graduated with a degree in Fine Arts. Audrey continued her ceramic arts education at the Ontario College of Art. While there\, she was awarded a scholarship which included a residency at the Instituto Allende in Mexico. Audrey’s work has been exhibited locally and internationally. She is inspired by the contrast in geometric and organic forms\, as well as ergonomic and practical forms of dishware. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/wheel-throwing-stoneware-beginner-winter-2027/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Wheel-Thumbnail-Fall.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Gardiner Museum 111 Queen's Park Toronto ON M5S 2C7 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=111 Queen's Park:geo:-79.3935128,43.6679938
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardinermuseum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-and-wheel-throwing-combo-intermediate-winter-2027/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270104T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270301T163000
DTSTAMP:20261105T194222Z
CREATED:20261103T214845Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261105T194222Z
UID:148414-1799069400-1803918600@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Hand Building and Wheel Throwing Combo (Intermediate)
DESCRIPTION:Hand Building and Wheel Throwing Combo (Intermediate)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Mondays January 4 to March 1\, 2027\n1:30 pm – 4:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    For ages 18+ \nLooking to build on your ceramics skills? Practice wheel-throwing and hand-building techniques and finish your pieces with glazing in this 8-week class designed for students with some previous clay experience. \nThis class includes a 10kg bag of clay\, and access to glazes and underglazes. Additional 10kg bags can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $412\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $485\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: January 4\, 11\, 18\, 25\, February 1\, 8\, 22\, March 1\nNo class February 15 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Week 1: Wheel throwing\nWeek 2: Trimming techniques and continuation of throwing\nWeek 3: Continuation of throwing and trimming\nWeek 4: Finish trimming and begin glazing\nWeek 5: Hand building\, pinch pots\, and attaching handles\nWeek 6: Coiling\nWeek 7: Studio time\nWeek 8: Glazing \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nUsing the pottery wheel may cause serious injury to a person who has a pacemaker. Consult a physician before use.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Salina Ladha\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Salina Ladha is a visual artist and educator with over 15 years of experience in the arts. She holds a BFA with a major in ceramics and a minor in painting. Her work has been exhibited across Canada and she has been a guest lecturer at Concordia University\, presenting on hand-building and ceramic practices. She brings a thoughtful\, hands-on approach to both her practice and instruction. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-and-wheel-throwing-combo-intermediate-winter-2027/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
