SUMMARY:Excel Basics 1: Create a Simple Spreadsheet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270108T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270108T143000
UID:6ae502179dbc2b002c923915@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Excel for absolute beginner
 s with little or no Excel experience.\nIn this first session\, you will:\n
 Learn the basic function and design of Excel files\nPractice basic data en
 try for text\, numbers\, and basic functions: Sum\, AutoSum and Average\nC
 reate and save your first workbook and worksheets\nUpon completion of this
  class\, you will be able to use Excel at a basic level.\nPrerequisites: B
 asic mouse and keyboard skills are required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demons
 trations\nDrop In
LOCATION:Maryvale\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae502179dbc2b002c923915
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardinermuseum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-beginner-winter-2027/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270108T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270226T163000
DTSTAMP:20261106T163544Z
CREATED:20261103T214727Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261106T163544Z
UID:148510-1799415000-1803659400@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Hand Building (Beginner)
DESCRIPTION:Hand Building (Beginner)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Fridays January 8 to February 26\, 2027\n1:30 pm – 4:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nFor ages 18+ \nLearn to make functional\, sculptural\, and decorative pieces using hand-building techniques. Practice sculpting\, slab building\, coiling\, surface decoration\, and glazing. This 8-week class is designed for students new to ceramics. \n\nThis class includes a 10kg bag of clay\, and access to glazes and underglazes. Additional bags can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $412\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $485\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: January 8\, 15\, 22\, 29\, February 5\, 12\, 19\, 26 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Week 1: Slab building\nWeek 2: Coil building\nWeek 3: Surface decoration\nWeek 4: Pinch pot forms\nWeek 5: Using clay templates\nWeek 6: Applying underglaze\nWeek 7: Exploring functional and non-functional works\nWeek 8: Glazing \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Natalie Fisher\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Natalie is a passionate young artist with more than 15 years of experience teaching art to students of all ages. She is formally trained in drawing\, painting\, photography\, printmaking\, and sculpture. She recently received her Masters in Expressive Arts Therapy from the University of Hong Kong. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-beginner-winter-2027/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Hand-Building-Fall-2026.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Gardiner Museum 111 Queen's Park Toronto ON M5S 2C7 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=111 Queen's Park:geo:-79.3935128,43.6679938
END:VEVENT
