BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af1f3133c35b95bcb2ab797"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 4: Use Google Search and Maps
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270109T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270109T113000
UID:6af1f3133c35b95bcb2ab797@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A class on using Google's filters\, tools\, and Maps for absol
 ute beginners with little computer experience.\nIn this fourth session you
  will:\nUse Google search tools more effectively to find websites\, images
 \, and news sites\nExplore Google Maps to find addresses and get direction
 s for transit and road travel.\nUpon completion of this class students wil
 l be able to use more advanced search engine features and use Google Maps 
 at a basic level.\nPrerequisites: Computers for Beginners 1\, 2 & 3 or bas
 ic mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstr
 ations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this f
 orm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries 
 Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be use
 d for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions 
 about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerli
 ne staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toron
 to ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Learning Center
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af1f3133c35b95bcb2ab797
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b007d630ad4ed003a04a8d1"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Neighbourhood Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270109T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270109T113000
UID:6b007d630ad4ed003a04a8d1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy some light refreshments\, and friendly chat among other 
 Palmerston Library patrons. We will have chess and other board games avai
 lable.\nGet to know your neighbours and local library staff and let us kn
 ow what information and resources you would like to access at the library 
 and in the community.\nEach week\, staff will highlight services at the li
 brary that you may want to become more familiar with and answer any additi
 onal questions to make the most of you library membership. Feel free to br
 ing your own device to follow along as we walk through accessing these onl
 ine resources:\nJanuary 9 - E-books\, Digital Magazines and Newspapers\nJ
 anuary 16 - Digital Movies and Music\nJanuary 23 - Museum and Arts Passes\
 nJanuary 30 - eLearning\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all part
 icipants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b007d630ad4ed003a04a8d1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
