SUMMARY:Stabbed Through the Heart Cross Stitch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270116T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270116T153000
UID:6afddb99be8bbf00683be9fd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Merril Collection for an introductory cross sti
 tch workshop. Participants will stitch a romantasy-inspired heart impaled 
 by a sword. Enjoy our current exhibit\,\nLove\, Lust and Lore\n\, and lear
 n a new skill. This workshop is designed for beginners with no sewing or 
 cross stitch experience. All supplies will be provided.\nThis workshop wil
 l be offered on two different dates. Please only register for one. Walk-i
 ns will be welcome if the program is not full.\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Merril Collection Reading Room\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afddb99be8bbf00683be9fd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b006f0a92dc1500457c81e3"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Maintaining an Engaging and Enjoyable Backyard During the Winter S
 eason: Strategies for Feeding Birds in Colder Months (Drop-in)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270116T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270116T150000
UID:6b006f0a92dc1500457c81e3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:When temperatures drop and natural food becomes less available
 \, it's important to keep your backyard welcoming for birds. By adjusting 
 your feeding habits during colder months\, you can make winter feeding eas
 ier for yourself and help maintain a lively outdoor space that brings you 
 daily pleasure.\n"Presented by Jim Mackiewicz who is the owner of Wild Bi
 rds Unlimited and has been helping customers with backyard bird feeding an
 d connecting to nature for 25 years\; Certified Bird Feeding Specialist\; 
 Garden Design Certificate from George Brown College\; Graduate of LEAF Tre
 e Tenders Volunteer Program\; Pollinator Stewardship Certification\; Certi
 fied Instructor in Project Wild/Project Zero\; Canadian Federal Government
  Permit for Ornithological Research - Banding Birds"
LOCATION:Queen/Saulter
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b006f0a92dc1500457c81e3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
