SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270118T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270118T150000
UID:6afe3df10f200f185985ace5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nJoin us at the crafts & games ta
 ble\, or for a community walk (weather permitting).\nVisit with a therapy 
 dog!\nOzzy is here\nNovember 9\, 23 + December 7\, 21.\nSnacks and refres
 hments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be availa
 ble at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisi
 s Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afe3df10f200f185985ace5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aeb78359dbc2b002c935c1b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Word Basics 3: Basic Resumes with Word
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270118T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270118T150000
UID:6aeb78359dbc2b002c935c1b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Practice your Microsoft Word skills while creating a simple re
 sume.\nIn this class\, you will:\nFormat a simple resume\nPractice advance
 d formatting using Ruler Tools and Format Painter\nUse Grammar and Spell c
 heck tools\nPractice using Word’s built-in resume templates\nSave docume
 nts in other formats such as PDF\nUpon completion of this class\, you will
  be able to create an organized simple resume and access resume templates 
 with additional style options.\nPrerequisites: Word Basics 1 & 2 or equiva
 lent skills. Keyboarding and mouse skills are required.\nInformation Colle
 ction Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the T
 oronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20
 (c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program r
 egistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library han
 dles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@t
 pl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Cliffcrest
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aeb78359dbc2b002c935c1b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
