X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 6: Use Gmail
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270123T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270123T113000
UID:6af1f3e7f9d28050ccb23d92@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to use Gmail\, Google’s free web-based email service.\
 nIn this sixth session you will:\nPractice basic email functions: send\, r
 ead\, reply\, forward\, delete email\, and attach files\nReview how spam a
 nd junk mail work\nUpon completion of this class students will have a basi
 c understanding of how to use email.\nInstructions on how to set up and ma
 nage your own free Gmail account are included in the handout.\nPrerequisit
 es: Basic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with de
 monstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Learning Center
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af1f3e7f9d28050ccb23d92
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b007d630ad4ed003a04a8d3"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Neighbourhood Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270123T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270123T113000
UID:6b007d630ad4ed003a04a8d3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy some light refreshments\, and friendly chat among other 
 Palmerston Library patrons. We will have chess and other board games avai
 lable.\nGet to know your neighbours and local library staff and let us kn
 ow what information and resources you would like to access at the library 
 and in the community.\nEach week\, staff will highlight services at the li
 brary that you may want to become more familiar with and answer any additi
 onal questions to make the most of you library membership. Feel free to br
 ing your own device to follow along as we walk through accessing these onl
 ine resources:\nJanuary 9 - E-books\, Digital Magazines and Newspapers\nJ
 anuary 16 - Digital Movies and Music\nJanuary 23 - Museum and Arts Passes\
 nJanuary 30 - eLearning\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all part
 icipants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b007d630ad4ed003a04a8d3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
