BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Preschool": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a21a73a46d5f64f7dcdeff6"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_preschool
SUMMARY:Saturday Movie: The Girl Who Cried Pearls and Higglety Piggley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270123T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270123T160000
UID:6a21a73a46d5f64f7dcdeff6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Due to Hillcrest Library closure on July 27\, this event will
  be postponed until January 2027.\nIn Montreal\, at the dawn of the 20th c
 entury\, a poor boy falls in love with a girl whose sorrow turns into pear
 ls. He sells them to a ruthless pawnbroker\, who hungers for more. Tempted
  by greed\, the boy must choose between love and fortune. The choice could
  damn his soul.\nThe 2026 Oscar® Winner for Best Animated Short Film from
  the acclaimed team of Chris Lavis and Maciek Szczerbowski. This meticulo
 usly crafted film is a testament to the magic of stop-motion animation. Wi
 th handmade puppets\, mesmerizing narration by Colm Feore and a haunting s
 core by Patrick Watson\,\nThe Girl Who Cried Pearls\nis a timeless parable
  of desire\, deception and the price of innocence. (25 minutes)\nAlso scre
 ening from the same Oscar winning team with be\nHigglety Pigglety Pop! or 
 There Must Be More to Life\n. This live-action/animated adaptation of Maur
 ice Sendak's book features the voices of Meryl Streep and Forest Whitaker.
 \nThe story follows Jennie the terrier's suspenseful and unexpectedly mo
 ving journey to gain new experiences and realize her dream of becoming the
  star of the World Mother Goose Theatre. (23 minutes)\nFilms courtesy of t
 he National Film Board of Canada (NFB).\nDrop-in! No registration required
 .
LOCATION:Hillcrest\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a21a73a46d5f64f7dcdeff6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afdd3e104009d003389612f"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Investing 101: What you need to know
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270123T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270123T150000
UID:6afdd3e104009d003389612f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Whether you are starting out or learning more about your curre
 nt investments\, this seminar will help you make sense of the complex worl
 d of investing. We will cover the three asset classes: stocks\, bonds\, an
 d cash plus simple ways to get started with investing. In this easy-to-und
 erstand seminar\, Teri will set out the advantages of each of the three ma
 jor tax-sheltered investing plans for Canadians: Tax-Free Savings Accounts
  (TFSAs)\, Registered Retirement Savings Plans (RRSPs) and the new First H
 ome Savings Accounts (FHSAs).\nPresented by Teri Courchene\, BA\, MA\, ME
 d\, CSC\nTeri earned master’s degrees in economics and in education.  In
  her earlier career as an economist\, she was Director of Economic Researc
 h at a major bank. In her second career\, Teri taught at her own small Mon
 tessori school for 10 years\, then switched to tutoring students in math. 
 In her third career\, she taught investing for 5 years at the University o
 f Toronto School of Continuing Studies.\nRegistration is encouraged\n. Dro
 p-ins are welcome until capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection Notic
 e:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your i
 nformation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 4
 16-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Hillcrest\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afdd3e104009d003389612f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
