DESCRIPTION:Drop in and expand your mind with Leaside's monthly book club.
  Come together to share your thoughts and opinions about the book in a fri
 endly and cozy environment.\nPick up the upcoming month's book at the Leas
 ide branch circulation desk or at each book club session\nDate and Title:\
 n27 January\n–\nThe siren's call: How attention became the world's most 
 endangered resource by Chris Hayes\n24 February\n-\nThe innocent man by Jo
 hn Grisham\n24 March\n-\nAuthor Talk **\nTBA**\n28 April\n-\nLessons for l
 iving: What only adversity can teach you by Phil Stutz\n26 May\n-\nThe sh
 ock doctrine by Naomi Klein\n30 June\n-\nEducated by Tara Westover\n29 Sep
 tember\n-\nBlack Pill: How I witnessed the darkest corners of the internet
  come to life\, poison society\, and capture American politics by Elle Re
 eve\n27 October\n-\nThe wager: A tale of shipwreck\, mutiny and murder by
  David Grann\n24 November\n-\nThe backyard bird chronicles by Amy Tan\n22 
 December\n-\nThe wide wide sea by Hampton Sides\nPlease Note:\nBook club w
 ill be paused during the summer and will resume again in the fall
LOCATION:Leaside
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afca014e2267c00335d04cc
