SUMMARY:Author Talk: An Afternoon with Marianne Miller
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270127T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270127T150000
UID:6afa1695899b61003313d7ff@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Marianne K. Miller presents her historical novel\,\nWe Were Th
 e Bullfighters\n(2024\, Dundurn Press). Focusing on Ernest Hemingway's 
 time working for The Toronto Daily Star in 1923\, the story stems from hi
 s first day\, when he is sent to cover notorious bank robber Red Ryan’s
  escape from Kingston Penitentiary.\nNo registration required\, drop in!
LOCATION:Wychwood\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afa1695899b61003313d7ff
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
