SUMMARY:After School Club: Puppet Crafts - Make a Paper Puppet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270202T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270202T170000
UID:6ae8e25a96ec3a003adec6b9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Making puppets should be fun\, cheap and easy! Mike Harding of
  Applefun Puppetry shows you how to make your own puppets and put on a sho
 w for your friends!\nIn this puppet-making workshop\, you will learn to us
 e materials readily available around the house to make puppets.\nRecommend
 ed materials:\nConstruction paper (or printer paper)\nSafety scissors\nGlu
 e stick\nMarkers\nScotch tape or masking tape\nOptional: stickers\, pom-po
 ms\, and yarn\nZ\noom URL to access the online program will be emailed to 
 registrants ahead of program date.\nThis online program is suitable for ch
 ildren ages 6-12. Younger children may require assistance from caregivers.
  It is recommended that parents or caregivers are present during this live
  program. Questions about online programs? Please email us at programpropo
 sals@tpl.ca.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae8e25a96ec3a003adec6b9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
